1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,337
What's today's video about? Planning a trip!

2
00:00:07,337 --> 00:00:08,837
Scene 1: Planning a Relaxing Hot Spring Getaway

3
00:00:08,837 --> 00:00:12,875
How about a weekend trip to a hot spring?

4
00:00:12,898 --> 00:00:16,265
I’ve been so tired lately.

5
00:00:16,287 --> 00:00:18,055
That sounds great!

6
00:00:18,079 --> 00:00:20,974
I’d love to relax and unwind too.

7
00:00:20,997 --> 00:00:26,641
I can’t decide between Hakone and Izu—what do you think?

8
00:00:26,665 --> 00:00:28,465
Hmm, let me think.

9
00:00:28,488 --> 00:00:32,344
Hakone is closer than Izu, though.

10
00:00:32,368 --> 00:00:38,455
But Izu has stunning views, and you can enjoy delicious seafood.

11
00:00:38,478 --> 00:00:41,933
Then why don’t we try Izu?

12
00:00:41,957 --> 00:00:44,253
Yeah, let’s do that.

13
00:00:44,276 --> 00:00:46,409
Should we go by train?

14
00:00:46,432 --> 00:00:51,632
I think driving would be more convenient than taking the train.

15
00:00:51,655 --> 00:00:55,137
But the roads might be crowded on the weekend.

16
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:57,094
True, you’re right.

17
00:00:57,117 --> 00:01:00,556
Plus, if we take the train, we can enjoy some drinks.

18
00:01:00,579 --> 00:01:03,512
Alright, let’s go by train then.

19
00:01:03,535 --> 00:01:06,669
I’ll book the tickets in advance.

20
00:01:06,692 --> 00:01:08,258
Thanks so much!

21
00:01:08,281 --> 00:01:10,856
What about the hotel?

22
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:13,913
I’d love a hotel with an ocean view.

23
00:01:13,936 --> 00:01:16,915
I’ll look it up online.

24
00:01:16,939 --> 00:01:19,872
Should we have dinner at the hotel?

25
00:01:19,895 --> 00:01:23,666
I think eating outside the hotel would be cheaper.

26
00:01:23,690 --> 00:01:29,293
I’ll check if there are any good restaurants nearby.

27
00:01:29,317 --> 00:01:30,732
That would be a big help!

28
00:01:30,756 --> 00:01:34,922
I want to soak in the hot springs twice—once at night and once in the morning.

29
00:01:34,945 --> 00:01:36,679
That sounds great!

30
00:01:36,702 --> 00:01:40,635
A nice, big bath will really help melt the stress away.

31
00:01:40,658 --> 00:01:45,673
I’d like to buy some souvenirs, so I’ll bring a little extra cash.

32
00:01:45,697 --> 00:01:48,863
I want to get some dried fish.

33
00:01:48,886 --> 00:01:53,154
Then let’s visit the market on Sunday morning.

34
00:01:53,177 --> 00:01:54,832
That sounds fun!

35
00:01:54,856 --> 00:01:57,856
What time should we leave?

36
00:01:57,879 --> 00:02:01,969
It’d be best to leave early in the morning, right?

37
00:02:01,993 --> 00:02:03,932
How about 8 o’clock?

38
00:02:03,955 --> 00:02:06,040
Sounds good.

39
00:02:06,063 --> 00:02:09,557
Let’s meet at the ticket gates in Tokyo Station.

40
00:02:09,581 --> 00:02:12,278
Don’t be late, okay?

41
00:02:12,302 --> 00:02:13,971
Don’t worry, I won’t be.

42
00:02:13,994 --> 00:02:16,794
I’ll set an alarm just in case.

43
00:02:16,817 --> 00:02:20,656
I’ll let you know once I’ve booked the hotel.

44
00:02:20,679 --> 00:02:22,162
Thanks, I appreciate it.

45
00:02:22,186 --> 00:02:24,655
I’m really looking forward to this!

46
00:02:24,679 --> 00:02:26,212
Me too!

47
00:02:26,235 --> 00:02:31,242
Thinking about this trip makes me feel like I can power through work next week!

48
00:02:31,266 --> 00:02:34,645
Just make sure you don’t catch a cold before the trip!

49
00:02:34,669 --> 00:02:36,043
Thanks so much!

50
00:02:36,066 --> 00:02:38,000
Goodnight!

51
00:02:38,023 --> 00:02:47,032
You can download today’s video script from the description and top comment. Don’t forget to leave a comment before downloading!

52
00:02:47,032 --> 00:02:48,532
Scene 2: Planning an Adventure in Hokkaido

53
00:02:48,532 --> 00:02:53,065
I'm planning to visit Hokkaido during summer vacation.

54
00:02:53,088 --> 00:02:54,821
That sounds great!

55
00:02:54,844 --> 00:02:58,211
Where in Hokkaido are you going?

56
00:02:58,234 --> 00:03:02,673
I want to visit Sapporo, Otaru, and Furano.

57
00:03:02,697 --> 00:03:07,431
That might be a bit tight schedule-wise.

58
00:03:07,454 --> 00:03:09,187
Really?

59
00:03:09,210 --> 00:03:13,180
I thought three days would be enough to cover all of them.

60
00:03:13,204 --> 00:03:19,080
Hokkaido is really vast, so traveling between places takes time.

61
00:03:19,104 --> 00:03:23,739
I was thinking of getting around by train. What do you think?

62
00:03:23,762 --> 00:03:28,835
If you're heading to Furano, renting a car would be better.

63
00:03:28,859 --> 00:03:33,026
I'm not very good at driving, though.

64
00:03:33,049 --> 00:03:37,457
In that case, why not join a bus tour?

65
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:41,080
With a tour, I wouldn’t have to drive.

66
00:03:41,104 --> 00:03:45,437
Exactly—you can even sleep on the way to your destination!

67
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:50,727
By the way, can I take a train from Sapporo to Otaru?

68
00:03:50,750 --> 00:03:54,521
Yes, it takes about an hour by train.

69
00:03:54,545 --> 00:03:58,278
I want to try some delicious sushi in Otaru.

70
00:03:58,301 --> 00:04:02,997
Otaru has plenty of famous sushi spots!

71
00:04:03,021 --> 00:04:06,027
Do you know any places you’d recommend?

72
00:04:06,050 --> 00:04:08,816
I’ll ask my friend for suggestions.

73
00:04:08,839 --> 00:04:10,706
Thanks so much!

74
00:04:10,729 --> 00:04:14,862
I’m planning to try ramen in Sapporo.

75
00:04:14,885 --> 00:04:17,539
Miso ramen is a must-try!

76
00:04:17,562 --> 00:04:21,162
I’m also planning to visit the flower fields in Furano.

77
00:04:21,185 --> 00:04:22,823
That sounds amazing!

78
00:04:22,847 --> 00:04:24,903
Are they lavender fields?

79
00:04:24,926 --> 00:04:28,360
Yes, they’re supposed to be stunning.

80
00:04:28,383 --> 00:04:31,639
Make sure to take lots of photos!

81
00:04:31,663 --> 00:04:33,632
Of course!

82
00:04:33,656 --> 00:04:36,132
What should I bring back as souvenirs?

83
00:04:36,156 --> 00:04:39,132
Shiroi Koibito, please!

84
00:04:39,156 --> 00:04:40,831
Sounds good.

85
00:04:40,854 --> 00:04:43,787
I’ll make a note so I don’t forget.

86
00:04:43,810 --> 00:04:46,545
Have you booked your hotel yet?

87
00:04:46,569 --> 00:04:49,211
No, not yet.

88
00:04:49,234 --> 00:04:51,603
You should book it soon.

89
00:04:51,626 --> 00:04:55,662
Summer vacation gets really busy, so it’s best to hurry.

90
00:04:55,686 --> 00:04:59,086
I’ll book it as soon as I get home today.

91
00:04:59,109 --> 00:05:06,214
You can review today’s video with the link in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

92
00:05:06,214 --> 00:05:07,714
Scene 3: Planning a Kyoto Trip

93
00:05:07,714 --> 00:05:12,081
I’m traveling to Kyoto next month.

94
00:05:12,103 --> 00:05:14,503
Kyoto is wonderful!

95
00:05:14,526 --> 00:05:17,540
What are you planning to see?

96
00:05:17,564 --> 00:05:22,997
Kiyomizu-dera, Kinkaku-ji, and Fushimi Inari.

97
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:26,620
Are you planning to visit all of them in two days?

98
00:05:26,643 --> 00:05:28,243
Me too!

99
00:05:28,266 --> 00:05:31,870
But I might not have enough time.

100
00:05:31,894 --> 00:05:37,566
Kyoto’s roads get congested, so trains are better than buses.

101
00:05:37,589 --> 00:05:39,470
Is that so?

102
00:05:39,494 --> 00:05:42,831
I thought buses would be more convenient.

103
00:05:42,855 --> 00:05:46,351
It gets especially crowded in autumn.

104
00:05:46,374 --> 00:05:49,541
The subway would be faster.

105
00:05:49,564 --> 00:05:50,931
Sounds good.

106
00:05:50,954 --> 00:05:54,820
Where should I go on the first day?

107
00:05:54,843 --> 00:05:59,250
I recommend visiting Fushimi Inari early in the morning.

108
00:05:59,274 --> 00:06:02,840
Is it because it gets crowded during the day?

109
00:06:02,863 --> 00:06:04,397
Yes, that's right.

110
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:09,986
Plus, if you're taking photos, mornings are the best for beautiful shots.

111
00:06:10,009 --> 00:06:13,643
After that, we'll head to Kiyomizu-dera.

112
00:06:13,666 --> 00:06:16,466
What about lunch?

113
00:06:16,489 --> 00:06:20,155
I'd love to try some delicious matcha sweets.

114
00:06:20,178 --> 00:06:24,469
There's a famous café near Kiyomizu-dera.

115
00:06:24,493 --> 00:06:27,093
I'd love to check it out.

116
00:06:27,116 --> 00:06:29,767
Should we make a reservation?

117
00:06:29,790 --> 00:06:34,645
Check online to see if reservations are available.

118
00:06:34,668 --> 00:06:38,802
I'm thinking of visiting Kinkaku-ji on the second day.

119
00:06:38,825 --> 00:06:44,268
Kinkaku-ji is stunning in the evening when the sunlight reflects off it.

120
00:06:44,291 --> 00:06:46,491
That sounds amazing!

121
00:06:46,514 --> 00:06:50,081
I'd love to walk around in a kimono.

122
00:06:50,104 --> 00:06:54,879
You might need to book a kimono rental in advance.

123
00:06:54,902 --> 00:06:56,955
I see.

124
00:06:56,978 --> 00:07:00,378
I'll make a reservation before I forget.

125
00:07:00,401 --> 00:07:05,468
Just a heads-up, walking in a kimono might be a bit tiring.

126
00:07:05,491 --> 00:07:08,224
If I get tired, I'll just take a taxi.

127
00:07:08,247 --> 00:07:12,465
You can buy souvenirs at Kyoto Station.

128
00:07:12,489 --> 00:07:16,706
I'll grab some souvenirs at the station before heading back.

129
00:07:16,730 --> 00:07:19,396
I recommend trying Yatsuhashi.

130
00:07:19,419 --> 00:07:22,753
I've never bought it before, so I'll give it a try.

131
00:07:22,776 --> 00:07:25,576
I hope you have a fantastic trip!

132
00:07:25,599 --> 00:07:29,481
Yes, I'm really looking forward to it!

133
00:07:29,505 --> 00:07:31,005
Scene 4: Choosing the Perfect Hotel for Your Okinawa Getaway

134
00:07:31,005 --> 00:07:35,138
I'm looking for a hotel for my Okinawa trip.

135
00:07:35,161 --> 00:07:37,740
What kind of hotel are you looking for?

136
00:07:37,764 --> 00:07:41,897
I'd love an affordable hotel with an ocean view.

137
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:46,687
Hotels near the ocean might be a bit pricey.

138
00:07:46,710 --> 00:07:50,930
My budget is around 10,000 yen per night.

139
00:07:50,953 --> 00:07:55,624
There are plenty of budget-friendly hotels in Naha city.

140
00:07:55,647 --> 00:08:00,447
Can I walk to the ocean from hotels in the city?

141
00:08:00,470 --> 00:08:03,673
It's a bit far to walk.

142
00:08:03,696 --> 00:08:05,909
You'd need a car.

143
00:08:05,932 --> 00:08:10,899
I'm a bit nervous about driving since I don't drive often.

144
00:08:10,923 --> 00:08:15,412
In that case, a hotel near a monorail station would be convenient.

145
00:08:15,435 --> 00:08:20,002
I'm torn between convenience and the view.

146
00:08:20,025 --> 00:08:25,592
How about spending the day by the ocean and staying in the city at night?

147
00:08:25,615 --> 00:08:27,948
That sounds like a great idea!

148
00:08:27,971 --> 00:08:31,704
Plus, it's convenient for dinner.

149
00:08:31,728 --> 00:08:35,798
Naha has so many amazing restaurants.

150
00:08:35,821 --> 00:08:39,588
Should I have breakfast at the hotel?

151
00:08:39,611 --> 00:08:45,579
I think booking a plan with breakfast included would be more convenient.

152
00:08:45,603 --> 00:08:48,136
I found this hotel online.

153
00:08:48,159 --> 00:08:49,526
What do you think?

154
00:08:49,549 --> 00:08:54,682
It's close to the station, but the rooms look a bit small.

155
00:08:54,705 --> 00:08:59,279
I only need a place to sleep, so size doesn't matter to me.

156
00:08:59,302 --> 00:09:02,550
How about booking this hotel then?

157
00:09:02,573 --> 00:09:04,306
Hmm, let me think.

158
00:09:04,329 --> 00:09:07,863
I'll read some reviews before making a decision.

159
00:09:07,886 --> 00:09:10,022
That sounds great!

160
00:09:10,045 --> 00:09:14,978
Oh, it says here the staff are really friendly.

161
00:09:15,001 --> 00:09:17,801
That’s reassuring.

162
00:09:17,824 --> 00:09:20,065
I’ll go ahead and book it here.

163
00:09:20,089 --> 00:09:23,255
Have you bought your plane tickets yet?

164
00:09:23,278 --> 00:09:24,678
Me too!

165
00:09:24,701 --> 00:09:27,436
I got them two months ago.

166
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:30,340
They’re cheaper if you buy them early, right?

167
00:09:30,364 --> 00:09:33,830
I’m so relieved we got the hotel sorted.

168
00:09:33,853 --> 00:09:37,590
Don’t forget to pack your swimsuit!

169
00:09:37,613 --> 00:09:38,780
Me too!

170
00:09:38,803 --> 00:09:41,978
I think I’ll buy a new one.

171
00:09:42,001 --> 00:09:44,978
Have a safe trip!

172
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:46,568
Thanks so much!

173
00:09:46,591 --> 00:09:48,806
I’ll have a blast!

174
00:09:48,829 --> 00:09:50,329
Scene 5: Kanazawa Travel Guide – Your Perfect Getaway

175
00:09:50,329 --> 00:09:54,742
I’d love to go on my first domestic trip—any suggestions, senpai?

176
00:09:54,766 --> 00:09:56,421
That sounds great!

177
00:09:56,444 --> 00:09:59,341
What kind of place are you looking for?

178
00:09:59,364 --> 00:10:04,642
Somewhere with amazing seafood and a peaceful vibe.

179
00:10:04,666 --> 00:10:07,884
How about Kanazawa?

180
00:10:07,908 --> 00:10:10,141
Kanazawa?

181
00:10:10,165 --> 00:10:12,298
What’s it like?

182
00:10:12,321 --> 00:10:16,695
It’s got these gorgeous old streets—so picturesque!

183
00:10:16,719 --> 00:10:19,485
Is the seafood really good there?

184
00:10:19,508 --> 00:10:20,842
Absolutely!

185
00:10:20,865 --> 00:10:25,242
You can feast on fresh sushi and seafood bowls at the market.

186
00:10:25,265 --> 00:10:28,037
That sounds amazing!

187
00:10:28,061 --> 00:10:31,828
How do I get there from Tokyo?

188
00:10:31,851 --> 00:10:34,538
You can take the Shinkansen.

189
00:10:34,561 --> 00:10:37,254
How long does it take?

190
00:10:37,278 --> 00:10:40,245
About two and a half hours.

191
00:10:40,268 --> 00:10:42,802
That’s closer than I thought!

192
00:10:42,825 --> 00:10:46,792
There’s also Kenrokuen, one of Japan’s most famous gardens.

193
00:10:46,815 --> 00:10:50,548
Strolling through a garden sounds so relaxing.

194
00:10:50,571 --> 00:10:54,818
Oh, and they have this famous ice cream with gold leaf on top!

195
00:10:54,842 --> 00:10:57,087
Gold leaf?

196
00:10:57,110 --> 00:10:59,044
I’ve got to try that!

197
00:10:59,067 --> 00:11:04,433
It rains a lot there, so bring an umbrella.

198
00:11:04,456 --> 00:11:07,824
I’ll toss a foldable one in my bag.

199
00:11:07,847 --> 00:11:12,181
There are some hidden-gem museums too—you should check them out!

200
00:11:12,204 --> 00:11:14,937
I love visiting museums!

201
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:19,760
I’ll tell you about my favorite ryokan—I always stay there.

202
00:11:19,783 --> 00:11:21,618
Really?

203
00:11:21,641 --> 00:11:23,208
Thanks so much!

204
00:11:23,231 --> 00:11:27,070
Their meals are incredible!

205
00:11:27,093 --> 00:11:29,929
I can’t wait to go now!

206
00:11:29,953 --> 00:11:35,604
By the way, if you go in winter, the crab is out of this world!

207
00:11:35,628 --> 00:11:42,261
I *love* crab, so I’ll have to plan a winter trip next time!

208
00:11:42,284 --> 00:11:46,525
You should book your Shinkansen tickets early too.

209
00:11:46,548 --> 00:11:47,847
Absolutely!

210
00:11:47,871 --> 00:11:51,871
Once I finalize my schedule, I’ll head to the station right away.

211
00:11:51,894 --> 00:11:55,894
If you have any questions, just ask anytime!

212
00:11:55,917 --> 00:11:57,451
Thanks so much!

213
00:11:57,474 --> 00:11:59,940
You’ve been a huge help!

214
00:11:59,963 --> 00:12:01,463
Scene 6: Beat the Crowds – The Early Bird’s Guide to Theme Parks

215
00:12:01,463 --> 00:12:05,297
Want to hit up a theme park this weekend?

216
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:08,007
I'd love to go!

217
00:12:08,030 --> 00:12:12,030
But weekends get so crowded, don't they?

218
00:12:12,053 --> 00:12:16,886
I'm thinking of going early before the park opens.

219
00:12:16,909 --> 00:12:20,343
What time are you planning to leave in the morning?

220
00:12:20,366 --> 00:12:23,766
How about leaving home at six?

221
00:12:23,789 --> 00:12:26,283
That's early!

222
00:12:26,306 --> 00:12:30,840
But that way, we can ride more attractions.

223
00:12:30,863 --> 00:12:34,829
I want to be the first in line for the popular roller coasters.

224
00:12:34,852 --> 00:12:37,823
Do you already have tickets?

225
00:12:37,847 --> 00:12:39,890
Not yet.

226
00:12:39,913 --> 00:12:43,350
I'll buy them online tomorrow.

227
00:12:43,374 --> 00:12:46,815
You should download the park's app too.

228
00:12:46,839 --> 00:12:50,486
What are the perks of having the app?

229
00:12:50,510 --> 00:12:54,043
You can get FastPasses through the app.

230
00:12:54,066 --> 00:12:56,433
That's super convenient!

231
00:12:56,456 --> 00:12:58,742
I'll download it right away.

232
00:12:58,765 --> 00:13:01,570
What about lunch?

233
00:13:01,593 --> 00:13:03,993
The restaurants will be packed too.

234
00:13:04,016 --> 00:13:07,862
Let's eat around eleven before it gets busy.

235
00:13:07,886 --> 00:13:12,619
I'll check if we can make a reservation at a restaurant.

236
00:13:12,642 --> 00:13:14,313
Thanks, I appreciate it.

237
00:13:14,336 --> 00:13:17,607
I want to stay until the night parade.

238
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:22,997
It might get chilly at night, so you should bring a jacket.

239
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:26,953
I'm planning to wear comfy shoes.

240
00:13:26,976 --> 00:13:30,709
You walk a lot in theme parks.

241
00:13:30,732 --> 00:13:34,205
If we get tired, let's take a break at a café.

242
00:13:34,229 --> 00:13:37,806
Walking around with popcorn is fun too!

243
00:13:37,830 --> 00:13:40,967
I heard they have popcorn in so many flavors.

244
00:13:40,990 --> 00:13:44,240
I love caramel flavor.

245
00:13:44,264 --> 00:13:46,939
I prefer the salty one.

246
00:13:46,962 --> 00:13:48,810
Let's get both!

247
00:13:48,833 --> 00:13:51,070
Are we taking the train,

248
00:13:51,093 --> 00:13:53,093
or driving?

249
00:13:53,117 --> 00:13:56,491
Driving might be less tiring.

250
00:13:56,515 --> 00:13:59,735
Then I'll drive.

251
00:13:59,758 --> 00:14:01,527
Really?

252
00:14:01,551 --> 00:14:03,084
Thanks so much!

253
00:14:03,107 --> 00:14:06,507
I should fill up the gas tank.

254
00:14:06,530 --> 00:14:09,497
I can't wait for the weekend!

255
00:14:09,519 --> 00:14:11,019
Scene 7: Osaka Food Adventure

256
00:14:11,019 --> 00:14:17,297
I want to eat so many delicious things in Osaka!

257
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:20,720
In Osaka, takoyaki and okonomiyaki are a must.

258
00:14:20,743 --> 00:14:24,614
I definitely want to try kushikatsu too.

259
00:14:24,637 --> 00:14:28,437
Are you planning to eat all of that in one day?

260
00:14:28,460 --> 00:14:32,142
Yep, I'll go on an empty stomach!

261
00:14:32,166 --> 00:14:38,332
Dotonbori has all those restaurants in one place.

262
00:14:38,355 --> 00:14:42,795
First, I want to walk around eating takoyaki.

263
00:14:42,818 --> 00:14:48,585
Food crawls are fun, but be careful not to burn yourself.

264
00:14:48,608 --> 00:14:52,216
Freshly made ones are really hot.

265
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:56,921
After takoyaki, let's have okonomiyaki.

266
00:14:56,944 --> 00:15:01,478
I heard people eat okonomiyaki with rice.

267
00:15:01,501 --> 00:15:05,434
That's what locals do, apparently.

268
00:15:05,457 --> 00:15:09,148
That's a lot of carbs!

269
00:15:09,171 --> 00:15:14,665
You can forget about your diet while traveling.

270
00:15:14,689 --> 00:15:18,422
You're right. I'm planning to eat a lot.

271
00:15:18,445 --> 00:15:22,692
Let's grab some beer at a kushikatsu place tonight.

272
00:15:22,716 --> 00:15:27,249
You know you can't double-dip the kushikatsu sauce, right?

273
00:15:27,272 --> 00:15:31,140
We’ve got to follow the rules when eating it.

274
00:15:31,164 --> 00:15:35,534
Should we make a reservation at the kushikatsu place?

275
00:15:35,557 --> 00:15:40,933
Popular spots get crowded, so it’s better to book ahead.

276
00:15:40,956 --> 00:15:45,190
Alright, I’ll make the reservation online.

277
00:15:45,213 --> 00:15:49,679
Do you know a place with amazing pork buns?

278
00:15:49,702 --> 00:15:52,585
Are you talking about that famous spot in Namba?

279
00:15:52,609 --> 00:15:56,642
Yeah, there’s always a line there.

280
00:15:56,665 --> 00:15:59,999
I’d love to grab some as souvenirs too.

281
00:16:00,022 --> 00:16:04,288
We can just keep them in the hotel fridge.

282
00:16:04,311 --> 00:16:08,345
We could even have them for breakfast the next day.

283
00:16:08,368 --> 00:16:12,734
I’m a little worried I’ll eat too much and get a stomachache.

284
00:16:12,757 --> 00:16:16,290
Don’t worry, I’ll bring some stomach medicine.

285
00:16:16,313 --> 00:16:18,947
That’s a relief!

286
00:16:18,970 --> 00:16:21,543
Let’s go on an all-you-can-eat food tour!

287
00:16:21,566 --> 00:16:24,166
I’m getting excited just thinking about it!

288
00:16:24,189 --> 00:16:25,689
Scene 8: Alternative Plans for Rainy Days

289
00:16:25,689 --> 00:16:30,662
Looks like the weather won’t cooperate for our weekend camping trip.

290
00:16:30,686 --> 00:16:33,286
Did you check the forecast?

291
00:16:33,309 --> 00:16:38,443
Yeah, it’s supposed to rain on Saturday.

292
00:16:38,466 --> 00:16:41,961
Camping in the rain sounds like a hassle.

293
00:16:41,984 --> 00:16:46,817
If it rains, should we go somewhere else instead?

294
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:50,914
Where should we go instead of camping?

295
00:16:50,938 --> 00:16:56,477
An aquarium or museum would be great—no rain, no problem!

296
00:16:56,501 --> 00:16:59,278
I’d love to go to the aquarium.

297
00:16:59,301 --> 00:17:01,435
I want to see the dolphins!

298
00:17:01,458 --> 00:17:06,091
There’s a big aquarium nearby, actually.

299
00:17:06,114 --> 00:17:09,124
Let’s go there, then.

300
00:17:09,147 --> 00:17:14,123
If it rains, we’ll have to cancel the campsite.

301
00:17:14,146 --> 00:17:17,680
When does the cancellation fee kick in?

302
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:23,744
We shouldn’t be charged if we cancel three days in advance, so let’s wait and see.

303
00:17:23,767 --> 00:17:25,252
Hmm, let me think.

304
00:17:25,275 --> 00:17:29,152
The forecast might change, after all.

305
00:17:29,175 --> 00:17:33,412
If it’s sunny, we’ll go camping as planned.

306
00:17:33,436 --> 00:17:37,203
What about the aquarium tickets?

307
00:17:37,226 --> 00:17:41,393
I think we can buy them at the counter on the day.

308
00:17:41,416 --> 00:17:44,622
Either way, I’m excited!

309
00:17:44,645 --> 00:17:49,378
Just in case, I won’t pack lunch.

310
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:53,448
Are there any good restaurants near the aquarium?

311
00:17:53,472 --> 00:17:57,238
I heard there’s an Italian place nearby.

312
00:17:57,261 --> 00:18:00,028
I’d love to try their pizza!

313
00:18:00,051 --> 00:18:04,217
Let’s prepare so we can still have fun, rain or shine.

314
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:07,840
We should bring umbrellas and towels, just in case.

315
00:18:07,863 --> 00:18:12,761
We’re driving, so we can bring as much as we want.

316
00:18:12,785 --> 00:18:15,551
I’ll pick you up.

317
00:18:15,574 --> 00:18:17,208
Thanks so much!

318
00:18:17,231 --> 00:18:19,571
Let’s meet at 9.

319
00:18:19,594 --> 00:18:24,493
We’ll check the weather again Friday night.

320
00:18:24,516 --> 00:18:26,083
Me too!

321
00:18:26,106 --> 00:18:28,243
Sounds good—thanks!

322
00:18:28,266 --> 00:18:29,766
Scene 9: Road Trip to Mt. Fuji – Let’s Hit the Road!

323
00:18:29,766 --> 00:18:33,810
Let’s go for a drive near Mt. Fuji!

324
00:18:33,833 --> 00:18:35,200
That sounds great!

325
00:18:35,223 --> 00:18:37,869
Whose car should we take?

326
00:18:37,892 --> 00:18:40,980
I’ll bring mine.

327
00:18:41,004 --> 00:18:45,137
I can drive too, so let’s take turns along the way.

328
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:46,847
That would be a big help!

329
00:18:46,871 --> 00:18:49,738
Let’s take the highway.

330
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:53,927
I want to stop by Ebina Service Area on the way.

331
00:18:53,950 --> 00:18:57,396
Their melon pan is famous, right?

332
00:18:57,419 --> 00:18:58,986
Me too!

333
00:18:59,009 --> 00:19:01,976
I want to buy some and eat it in the car.

334
00:19:01,999 --> 00:19:04,732
Let’s grab some coffee too.

335
00:19:04,755 --> 00:19:08,955
Where should we go around Mt. Fuji?

336
00:19:08,978 --> 00:19:13,978
I’m thinking of going to Lake Kawaguchiko to take photos of Mt. Fuji.

337
00:19:14,001 --> 00:19:16,016
Hope it’s sunny!

338
00:19:16,039 --> 00:19:20,095
I want to try *houtou* for lunch.

339
00:19:20,119 --> 00:19:23,735
It’s warm and delicious, isn’t it?

340
00:19:23,758 --> 00:19:27,292
I’ll set the GPS to a famous *houtou* restaurant.

341
00:19:27,315 --> 00:19:30,054
Can we stop by a roadside station too?

342
00:19:30,077 --> 00:19:31,444
Me too!

343
00:19:31,466 --> 00:19:35,200
I plan to buy fresh veggies at the roadside station.

344
00:19:35,223 --> 00:19:39,118
It’s always fun to check out local specialties!

345
00:19:39,141 --> 00:19:45,074
I’d love to hit an onsen on the way back—do we have time?

346
00:19:45,097 --> 00:19:49,264
I think we can squeeze in a day-trip onsen in the evening.

347
00:19:49,287 --> 00:19:53,320
Then I’d better bring a towel!

348
00:19:53,343 --> 00:19:56,681
I’ll bring an extra one too.

349
00:19:56,705 --> 00:19:59,841
Traffic might get heavy on the way back.

350
00:19:59,864 --> 00:20:03,998
We should leave early to avoid the rush.

351
00:20:04,021 --> 00:20:05,554
Hmm, let me think.

352
00:20:05,577 --> 00:20:09,344
Let’s aim to leave by 3 PM.

353
00:20:09,367 --> 00:20:12,533
Can I bring my favorite music CDs?

354
00:20:12,556 --> 00:20:14,808
Of course!

355
00:20:14,832 --> 00:20:17,365
Let’s listen to them on the drive!

356
00:20:17,388 --> 00:20:19,988
Let’s make sure to drive safely.

357
00:20:20,011 --> 00:20:21,245
Me too!

358
00:20:21,268 --> 00:20:24,688
I’ll be careful not to speed.

359
00:20:24,711 --> 00:20:27,591
I can’t wait for this weekend!

360
00:20:27,614 --> 00:20:30,547
Let’s make lots of memories!

361
00:20:30,570 --> 00:20:32,070
Scene 10: Final Pre-Trip Check – Don’t Forget Anything!

362
00:20:32,070 --> 00:20:35,404
Our trip starts tomorrow!

363
00:20:35,427 --> 00:20:36,427
Me too!

364
00:20:36,450 --> 00:20:39,923
Have you finished packing?

365
00:20:39,946 --> 00:20:42,319
Almost done!

366
00:20:42,343 --> 00:20:45,476
Let’s double-check what we’re bringing.

367
00:20:45,499 --> 00:20:49,132
Did you put your passport and tickets in your bag?

368
00:20:49,155 --> 00:20:50,522
Me too!

369
00:20:50,545 --> 00:20:54,878
Yep, I packed them first—they’re the most important!

370
00:20:54,901 --> 00:20:57,757
Who’s bringing the camera?

371
00:20:57,780 --> 00:21:01,947
I’ll bring my good one.

372
00:21:01,970 --> 00:21:05,840
Just don’t forget the charger!

373
00:21:05,863 --> 00:21:08,714
I’m charging it right now.

374
00:21:08,737 --> 00:21:12,182
I’ll bring the guidebook.

375
00:21:12,206 --> 00:21:13,617
Thanks, I appreciate it.

376
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:17,174
Can you print out the maps too?

377
00:21:17,197 --> 00:21:20,604
Already printed and filed!

378
00:21:20,628 --> 00:21:22,519
That would be a big help!

379
00:21:22,542 --> 00:21:25,835
Should we bring medicine?

380
00:21:25,858 --> 00:21:30,326
Cold and stomach meds would be good to have, just in case.

381
00:21:30,350 --> 00:21:34,117
I’ll pack them.

382
00:21:34,140 --> 00:21:36,828
I already bought snacks!

383
00:21:36,851 --> 00:21:40,051
I'm looking forward to eating on the go.

384
00:21:40,074 --> 00:21:44,208
It might be better to carry a little extra cash.

385
00:21:44,231 --> 00:21:49,164
Is it because some places might not accept credit cards?

386
00:21:49,187 --> 00:21:53,002
Yes, since we're planning to visit some rural areas.

387
00:21:53,026 --> 00:21:54,720
Sounds good.

388
00:21:54,743 --> 00:21:57,242
I'll withdraw some from the bank.

389
00:21:57,266 --> 00:22:00,999
Our meeting time tomorrow is 7 AM, right?

390
00:22:01,022 --> 00:22:02,356
Me too!

391
00:22:02,379 --> 00:22:05,379
Let's gather at the north exit of the station.

392
00:22:05,402 --> 00:22:08,935
We can't afford to oversleep.

393
00:22:08,958 --> 00:22:12,125
You should go to bed early tonight.

394
00:22:12,148 --> 00:22:13,399
Me too!

395
00:22:13,422 --> 00:22:16,897
I'll go to bed right after checking my luggage.

396
00:22:16,920 --> 00:22:21,254
Please double-check to make sure you haven't forgotten anything.

397
00:22:21,277 --> 00:22:23,753
It should be fine.

398
00:22:23,776 --> 00:22:26,817
Alright, see you at the station tomorrow.

399
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:28,607
Goodnight!

400
00:22:28,630 --> 00:22:30,763
Looking forward to tomorrow.

401
00:22:30,786 --> 00:22:33,028
Goodnight!

402
00:22:42,688 --> 00:22:44,188
Scene 1: Planning a Relaxing Hot Spring Getaway

403
00:22:44,188 --> 00:22:48,464
Listening Test

404
00:22:48,464 --> 00:22:53,537
How about a weekend trip to a hot spring?

405
00:22:53,537 --> 00:23:00,483
Vませんか = Won't you...? / Why don't we...?
週末 = weekend
温泉 = hot spring

406
00:23:00,506 --> 00:23:04,206
Listening Test

407
00:23:04,206 --> 00:23:08,545
I’ve been so tired lately.

408
00:23:08,545 --> 00:23:14,519
Vて = ...and (giving a reason or cause)
最近 = recently, lately
疲れる = get tired

409
00:23:14,543 --> 00:23:16,810
Listening Test

410
00:23:16,810 --> 00:23:19,344
That sounds great!

411
00:23:22,904 --> 00:23:26,171
Listening Test

412
00:23:26,171 --> 00:23:30,004
I’d love to relax and unwind too.

413
00:23:30,004 --> 00:23:35,271
Vたい = want to do
休む = rest, take time off

414
00:23:35,294 --> 00:23:41,032
Listening Test

415
00:23:41,032 --> 00:23:47,932
I can’t decide between Hakone and Izu—what do you think?

416
00:23:47,932 --> 00:23:57,279
N1 と N2 で = between N1 and N2
迷う = hesitate, be torn
どちら = which (of the two)

417
00:23:57,302 --> 00:23:59,568
Listening Test

418
00:23:59,568 --> 00:24:02,119
Hmm, let me think.

419
00:24:05,709 --> 00:24:09,842
Listening Test

420
00:24:09,842 --> 00:24:14,742
Hakone is closer than Izu, though.

421
00:24:14,742 --> 00:24:21,418
N1 のほうが N2 より = N1 is more ... than N2
近い (close) ↔ 遠い (far)

422
00:24:21,442 --> 00:24:27,575
Listening Test

423
00:24:27,575 --> 00:24:34,966
But Izu has stunning views, and you can enjoy delicious seafood.

424
00:24:34,966 --> 00:24:44,999
〜し、〜し = ..., and... (listing reasons)
景色 = scenery, view
魚 = fish

425
00:24:45,022 --> 00:24:48,789
Listening Test

426
00:24:48,789 --> 00:24:53,222
Then why don’t we try Izu?

427
00:24:53,222 --> 00:24:59,322
Vてみる = try doing
行く (go) ↔ 来る (come)

428
00:24:59,345 --> 00:25:02,061
Listening Test

429
00:25:02,061 --> 00:25:05,195
Yeah, let’s do that.

430
00:25:05,195 --> 00:25:09,528
Vましょう = Let's...

431
00:25:09,551 --> 00:25:12,118
Listening Test

432
00:25:12,118 --> 00:25:15,052
Should we go by train?

433
00:25:15,052 --> 00:25:19,125
N (means) + で = by / with N
電車 = train

434
00:25:19,148 --> 00:25:24,461
Listening Test

435
00:25:24,461 --> 00:25:30,848
I think driving would be more convenient than taking the train.

436
00:25:30,848 --> 00:25:39,519
N1 より N2 のほうが = N2 is more ... than N1
車 = car
便利 (convenient) ↔ 不便 (inconvenient)

437
00:25:39,542 --> 00:25:43,325
Listening Test

438
00:25:43,325 --> 00:25:47,798
But the roads might be crowded on the weekend.

439
00:25:47,798 --> 00:25:53,907
普通形 + かもしれません = might / may
道 = road, street
混む (be crowded) ↔ すく (be empty)

440
00:25:53,931 --> 00:25:56,305
Listening Test

441
00:25:56,305 --> 00:25:59,005
True, you’re right.

442
00:25:59,005 --> 00:26:02,757
確かに = certainly, surely

443
00:26:02,780 --> 00:26:06,534
Listening Test

444
00:26:06,534 --> 00:26:10,968
Plus, if we take the train, we can enjoy some drinks.

445
00:26:10,968 --> 00:26:17,034
N + なら = if it is N
お酒 = alcohol, sake
飲む = drink

446
00:26:17,057 --> 00:26:20,329
Listening Test

447
00:26:20,329 --> 00:26:24,163
Alright, let’s go by train then.

448
00:26:24,163 --> 00:26:29,429
Vる + ことにする = decide to do
決める = decide

449
00:26:29,452 --> 00:26:32,924
Listening Test

450
00:26:32,924 --> 00:26:36,991
I’ll book the tickets in advance.

451
00:26:36,991 --> 00:26:42,577
Vておく = do in advance
切符 = ticket
予約 = reservation

452
00:26:42,600 --> 00:26:44,667
Listening Test

453
00:26:44,667 --> 00:26:46,984
Thanks so much!

454
00:26:50,273 --> 00:26:53,240
Listening Test

455
00:26:53,240 --> 00:26:56,673
What about the hotel?

456
00:26:56,673 --> 00:27:01,419
N はどうしますか = What shall we do about N?
ホテル = hotel

457
00:27:01,443 --> 00:27:04,813
Listening Test

458
00:27:04,813 --> 00:27:08,767
I’d love a hotel with an ocean view.

459
00:27:08,767 --> 00:27:14,234
Vる + N = noun modifying (verb + noun)
海 = sea, ocean
見える = can be seen, be visible

460
00:27:14,257 --> 00:27:17,599
Listening Test

461
00:27:17,599 --> 00:27:21,507
I’ll look it up online.

462
00:27:21,507 --> 00:27:26,879
Vてみる = try doing
探す = search, look for

463
00:27:26,902 --> 00:27:30,202
Listening Test

464
00:27:30,202 --> 00:27:34,068
Should we have dinner at the hotel?

465
00:27:34,068 --> 00:27:39,368
N (place) + で = at / in N
晩ご飯 = dinner

466
00:27:39,391 --> 00:27:43,458
Listening Test

467
00:27:43,458 --> 00:27:48,256
I think eating outside the hotel would be cheaper.

468
00:27:48,256 --> 00:27:54,808
Vた + ほうがいい = had better do / it is better to do
外 (outside) ↔ 中 (inside)
安い (cheap) ↔ 高い (expensive)

469
00:27:54,831 --> 00:28:00,533
Listening Test

470
00:28:00,533 --> 00:28:07,400
I’ll check if there are any good restaurants nearby.

471
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:16,716
普通形 + かどうか = whether or not
近く (nearby) ↔ 遠く (far away)
調べる = check, investigate

472
00:28:16,740 --> 00:28:18,673
Listening Test

473
00:28:18,673 --> 00:28:20,806
That would be a big help!

474
00:28:20,806 --> 00:28:23,840
助かる = be helped, be saved

475
00:28:23,863 --> 00:28:28,239
Listening Test

476
00:28:28,239 --> 00:28:33,472
I want to soak in the hot springs twice—once at night and once in the morning.

477
00:28:33,472 --> 00:28:40,585
期間 + に + 回数 = ... times per period
夜 (night) ↔ 朝 (morning)
入る (enter, take a bath) ↔ 出る (exit, leave)

478
00:28:40,609 --> 00:28:42,809
Listening Test

479
00:28:42,809 --> 00:28:45,309
That sounds great!

480
00:28:48,832 --> 00:28:52,998
Listening Test

481
00:28:52,998 --> 00:28:57,934
A nice, big bath will really help melt the stress away.

482
00:28:57,934 --> 00:29:04,701
Vる + と = when / whenever (natural consequence)
広い (spacious) ↔ 狭い (narrow)
疲れが取れる = recover from fatigue

483
00:29:04,724 --> 00:29:09,898
Listening Test

484
00:29:09,898 --> 00:29:16,096
I’d like to buy some souvenirs, so I’ll bring a little extra cash.

485
00:29:16,096 --> 00:29:24,529
普通形 + ので = because / since
お土産 = souvenir
多い (many) ↔ 少ない (few)

486
00:29:24,552 --> 00:29:28,052
Listening Test

487
00:29:28,052 --> 00:29:32,153
I want to get some dried fish.

488
00:29:32,153 --> 00:29:37,787
Vたい = want to do
干物 = dried fish
買う (buy) ↔ 売る (sell)

489
00:29:37,810 --> 00:29:42,312
Listening Test

490
00:29:42,312 --> 00:29:47,663
Then let’s visit the market on Sunday morning.

491
00:29:47,663 --> 00:29:54,963
Vましょう = Let's...
日曜日 = Sunday
市場 = market

492
00:29:54,986 --> 00:29:57,126
Listening Test

493
00:29:57,126 --> 00:29:59,559
That sounds fun!

494
00:29:59,559 --> 00:30:02,930
いAそう = looks / sounds...
楽しい = fun, enjoyable

495
00:30:02,954 --> 00:30:06,300
Listening Test

496
00:30:06,300 --> 00:30:10,233
What time should we leave?

497
00:30:10,233 --> 00:30:15,603
何時にしますか = What time shall we make it?
出発 (departure) ↔ 到着 (arrival)

498
00:30:15,626 --> 00:30:19,964
Listening Test

499
00:30:19,964 --> 00:30:25,116
It’d be best to leave early in the morning, right?

500
00:30:25,116 --> 00:30:32,183
Vた + ほうがいい = had better do / it is better to do
早い (early) ↔ 遅い (late)

501
00:30:32,206 --> 00:30:34,639
Listening Test

502
00:30:34,639 --> 00:30:37,373
How about 8 o’clock?

503
00:30:37,373 --> 00:30:41,206
N はどうですか = How about N?
八時 = 8 o'clock

504
00:30:41,229 --> 00:30:43,762
Listening Test

505
00:30:43,762 --> 00:30:46,662
Sounds good.

506
00:30:46,662 --> 00:30:50,696
分かる = understand

507
00:30:50,719 --> 00:30:54,509
Listening Test

508
00:30:54,509 --> 00:30:58,975
Let’s meet at the ticket gates in Tokyo Station.

509
00:30:58,975 --> 00:31:05,111
Vましょう = Let's...
改札 = ticket gate
待ち合わせ = meeting, rendezvous

510
00:31:05,135 --> 00:31:08,235
Listening Test

511
00:31:08,235 --> 00:31:11,832
Don’t be late, okay?

512
00:31:11,832 --> 00:31:16,771
Vない + ようにする = try to / make sure to
遅れる (be late) ↔ 間に合う (be in time)

513
00:31:16,794 --> 00:31:18,952
Listening Test

514
00:31:18,952 --> 00:31:21,388
Don’t worry, I won’t be.

515
00:31:21,388 --> 00:31:24,783
大丈夫 = all right, okay

516
00:31:24,806 --> 00:31:27,976
Listening Test

517
00:31:27,976 --> 00:31:31,678
I’ll set an alarm just in case.

518
00:31:31,678 --> 00:31:36,752
Vておく = Do something in advance (e.g., 'Set the alarm clock')

519
00:31:36,776 --> 00:31:40,880
Listening Test

520
00:31:40,880 --> 00:31:45,747
I’ll let you know once I’ve booked the hotel.

521
00:31:45,747 --> 00:31:52,413
Vたら = If / Once (e.g., 'If you get in touch...')

522
00:31:52,436 --> 00:31:54,428
Listening Test

523
00:31:54,428 --> 00:31:56,662
Thanks, I appreciate it.

524
00:31:59,832 --> 00:32:02,708
Listening Test

525
00:32:02,708 --> 00:32:06,041
I’m really looking forward to this!

526
00:32:06,041 --> 00:32:10,640
楽しみ = Looking forward to something / Pleasure

527
00:32:10,664 --> 00:32:12,697
Me too!

528
00:32:12,720 --> 00:32:17,887
Listening Test

529
00:32:17,887 --> 00:32:24,070
Thinking about this trip makes me feel like I can power through work next week!

530
00:32:24,070 --> 00:32:32,503
Vそう = Looks like / Seems like (e.g., 'Looks like a fun trip!' or 'Seems like work is busy')

531
00:32:32,526 --> 00:32:36,226
Listening Test

532
00:32:36,226 --> 00:32:40,580
Just make sure you don’t catch a cold before the trip!

533
00:32:40,580 --> 00:32:46,557
Vない + ようにする = Try to / Make sure to (e.g., 'Try not to catch a cold' or 'Make sure to be careful')

534
00:32:46,580 --> 00:32:48,480
Listening Test

535
00:32:48,480 --> 00:32:50,580
Thanks so much!

536
00:32:53,588 --> 00:32:55,972
Listening Test

537
00:32:55,972 --> 00:32:58,689
Goodnight!

538
00:32:58,689 --> 00:33:02,474
おやすみなさい = Good night

539
00:33:02,498 --> 00:33:03,998
Scene 2: Planning an Adventure in Hokkaido

540
00:33:03,998 --> 00:33:08,698
Listening Test

541
00:33:08,698 --> 00:33:14,294
I'm planning to visit Hokkaido during summer vacation.

542
00:33:14,294 --> 00:33:21,960
Vる + つもり = Plan to (e.g., 'I plan to travel during summer vacation')

543
00:33:21,983 --> 00:33:24,167
Listening Test

544
00:33:24,167 --> 00:33:26,634
That sounds great!

545
00:33:30,124 --> 00:33:33,824
Listening Test

546
00:33:33,824 --> 00:33:38,160
Where in Hokkaido are you going?

547
00:33:38,160 --> 00:33:44,093
Vる + んですか = Asking for an explanation (e.g., 'Where are you going?')

548
00:33:44,117 --> 00:33:48,783
Listening Test

549
00:33:48,783 --> 00:33:54,322
I want to visit Sapporo, Otaru, and Furano.

550
00:33:54,322 --> 00:34:01,871
Vたい = Want to (e.g., 'I want to go')

551
00:34:01,895 --> 00:34:06,813
Listening Test

552
00:34:06,813 --> 00:34:12,683
That might be a bit tight schedule-wise.

553
00:34:12,683 --> 00:34:20,674
いA + かもしれません = Might be... (e.g., 'The schedule might be tight')

554
00:34:20,697 --> 00:34:22,931
Listening Test

555
00:34:22,931 --> 00:34:25,431
Really?

556
00:34:28,954 --> 00:34:33,187
Listening Test

557
00:34:33,187 --> 00:34:38,220
I thought three days would be enough to cover all of them.

558
00:34:38,220 --> 00:34:45,087
Vば = If... (e.g., 'If you finish everything in three days...')

559
00:34:45,110 --> 00:34:51,058
Listening Test

560
00:34:51,058 --> 00:34:58,225
Hokkaido is really vast, so traveling between places takes time.

561
00:34:58,225 --> 00:35:07,939
いA + から = Because... (e.g., 'Because it's spacious, moving is easy')

562
00:35:07,962 --> 00:35:12,795
Listening Test

563
00:35:12,795 --> 00:35:18,554
I was thinking of getting around by train. What do you think?

564
00:35:18,554 --> 00:35:26,389
Vよう + と思う = Plan / Intend to (e.g., 'I plan to go around by train')

565
00:35:26,413 --> 00:35:31,646
Listening Test

566
00:35:31,646 --> 00:35:37,913
If you're heading to Furano, renting a car would be better.

567
00:35:37,913 --> 00:35:46,415
Vた + 方がいい = Had better (e.g., 'You’d better borrow it instead of lending it')

568
00:35:46,439 --> 00:35:50,837
Listening Test

569
00:35:50,837 --> 00:35:56,070
I'm not very good at driving, though.

570
00:35:56,070 --> 00:36:03,204
あまり + なA + じゃない = Not very... (e.g., 'I’m not very good at driving')

571
00:36:03,228 --> 00:36:07,861
Listening Test

572
00:36:07,861 --> 00:36:13,365
In that case, why not join a bus tour?

573
00:36:13,365 --> 00:36:20,865
Vたら + どうですか = Why don’t you...? / How about...? (e.g., 'Why don’t you apply?')

574
00:36:20,888 --> 00:36:24,788
Listening Test

575
00:36:24,788 --> 00:36:29,421
With a tour, I wouldn’t have to drive.

576
00:36:29,421 --> 00:36:35,755
Vなくてもいい = Don’t have to (e.g., 'You don’t have to do it')

577
00:36:35,778 --> 00:36:40,311
Listening Test

578
00:36:40,311 --> 00:36:45,705
Exactly—you can even sleep on the way to your destination!

579
00:36:45,705 --> 00:36:53,052
Vている + 間に = While (e.g., 'While you’re on the way, let’s check the destination')

580
00:36:53,076 --> 00:36:58,474
Listening Test

581
00:36:58,474 --> 00:37:04,947
By the way, can I take a train from Sapporo to Otaru?

582
00:37:04,947 --> 00:37:13,746
N1 + から + N2 + まで = From N1 to N2 (e.g., 'From Tokyo to Osaka')

583
00:37:13,769 --> 00:37:17,836
Listening Test

584
00:37:17,836 --> 00:37:22,617
Yes, it takes about an hour by train.

585
00:37:22,617 --> 00:37:29,166
N + くらい = About / Approximately (e.g., 'About one hour')

586
00:37:29,190 --> 00:37:33,190
Listening Test

587
00:37:33,190 --> 00:37:37,923
I want to try some delicious sushi in Otaru.

588
00:37:37,923 --> 00:37:44,390
Vたい = Want to (e.g., 'I want to eat delicious sushi!')

589
00:37:44,413 --> 00:37:49,313
Listening Test

590
00:37:49,313 --> 00:37:55,146
Otaru has plenty of famous sushi spots!

591
00:37:55,146 --> 00:38:03,100
なA + な + N = [Na-adjective modifier] (e.g., 'A famous place with lots of flowers')

592
00:38:03,124 --> 00:38:06,491
Listening Test

593
00:38:06,491 --> 00:38:10,424
Do you know any places you’d recommend?

594
00:38:10,424 --> 00:38:15,857
Vて + います = [Continuous/resultant state] (e.g., 'This shop is highly recommended')

595
00:38:15,880 --> 00:38:19,014
Listening Test

596
00:38:19,014 --> 00:38:22,651
I’ll ask my friend for suggestions.

597
00:38:22,651 --> 00:38:27,684
Vて + おく = Do something in advance (e.g., 'Let me prepare in advance for my friend')

598
00:38:27,707 --> 00:38:30,040
Listening Test

599
00:38:30,040 --> 00:38:32,680
Thanks so much!

600
00:38:36,403 --> 00:38:40,753
Listening Test

601
00:38:40,753 --> 00:38:45,920
I’m planning to try ramen in Sapporo.

602
00:38:45,920 --> 00:38:52,986
Vよう + と思う = Plan / Intend to (e.g., 'I plan to visit the flower field')

603
00:38:53,009 --> 00:38:56,045
Listening Test

604
00:38:56,045 --> 00:38:59,579
Miso ramen is a must-try!

605
00:38:59,579 --> 00:39:04,445
N + がおすすめ = N is recommended (e.g., 'Miso soup is recommended!')

606
00:39:04,469 --> 00:39:08,369
Listening Test

607
00:39:08,369 --> 00:39:13,002
I’m also planning to visit the flower fields in Furano.

608
00:39:13,002 --> 00:39:19,302
Vる + 予定 = Plan to (e.g., 'I plan to visit the flower field')

609
00:39:19,325 --> 00:39:21,458
Listening Test

610
00:39:21,458 --> 00:39:23,846
That sounds amazing!

611
00:39:27,225 --> 00:39:29,725
Listening Test

612
00:39:29,725 --> 00:39:32,592
Are they lavender fields?

613
00:39:32,592 --> 00:39:36,558
N + ですか = Is it N? (e.g., 'Is this a field?')

614
00:39:36,581 --> 00:39:40,321
Listening Test

615
00:39:40,321 --> 00:39:44,755
Yes, they’re supposed to be stunning.

616
00:39:44,755 --> 00:39:50,821
なA + だそうだ = I heard that... (e.g., 'I heard it’s beautiful there')

617
00:39:50,844 --> 00:39:54,430
Listening Test

618
00:39:54,430 --> 00:39:58,664
Make sure to take lots of photos!

619
00:39:58,664 --> 00:40:04,449
Vて + ください = Please (e.g., 'Please take a photo')

620
00:40:04,472 --> 00:40:06,906
Listening Test

621
00:40:06,906 --> 00:40:09,685
Of course!

622
00:40:09,685 --> 00:40:13,551
もちろん = Of course

623
00:40:13,574 --> 00:40:16,474
Listening Test

624
00:40:16,474 --> 00:40:19,809
What should I bring back as souvenirs?

625
00:40:19,809 --> 00:40:24,443
何 + がいいですか = What would you like? (e.g., 'What souvenir would you like?')

626
00:40:24,466 --> 00:40:27,800
Listening Test

627
00:40:27,800 --> 00:40:31,700
Shiroi Koibito, please!

628
00:40:31,700 --> 00:40:37,053
N + をお願いします = N, please (e.g., 'A white one for my sweetheart, please')

629
00:40:37,076 --> 00:40:39,242
Listening Test

630
00:40:39,242 --> 00:40:41,676
Sounds good.

631
00:40:45,132 --> 00:40:48,402
Listening Test

632
00:40:48,402 --> 00:40:52,235
I’ll make a note so I don’t forget.

633
00:40:52,235 --> 00:40:57,502
Vない + ように = So that... not (e.g., 'Take notes so you don’t forget')

634
00:40:57,525 --> 00:41:00,641
Listening Test

635
00:41:00,641 --> 00:41:04,274
Have you booked your hotel yet?

636
00:41:04,274 --> 00:41:09,274
もう + Vました = Already did (e.g., 'I already made a reservation')

637
00:41:09,297 --> 00:41:12,333
Listening Test

638
00:41:12,333 --> 00:41:15,867
No, not yet.

639
00:41:15,867 --> 00:41:20,733
まだ = Not yet / Still

640
00:41:20,756 --> 00:41:23,548
Listening Test

641
00:41:23,548 --> 00:41:26,782
You should book it soon.

642
00:41:26,782 --> 00:41:31,248
Vないと = Have to / Must (e.g., 'I have to hurry!')

643
00:41:31,271 --> 00:41:35,571
Listening Test

644
00:41:35,571 --> 00:41:40,671
Summer vacation gets really busy, so it’s best to hurry.

645
00:41:40,671 --> 00:41:47,614
Vた + 方がいい = Had better (e.g., 'You’d better go early if it’s crowded')

646
00:41:47,637 --> 00:41:51,347
Listening Test

647
00:41:51,347 --> 00:41:55,714
I’ll book it as soon as I get home today.

648
00:41:55,714 --> 00:42:01,701
Vたら = When / After (e.g., 'When you get home today...')

649
00:42:01,724 --> 00:42:03,224
Scene 3: Planning a Kyoto Trip

650
00:42:03,224 --> 00:42:07,804
Listening Test

651
00:42:07,804 --> 00:42:13,271
I’m traveling to Kyoto next month.

652
00:42:13,271 --> 00:42:20,704
N + に + 行きます = Go for N (e.g., 'I’m going on a trip next month')

653
00:42:20,727 --> 00:42:23,561
Listening Test

654
00:42:23,561 --> 00:42:26,827
Kyoto is wonderful!

655
00:42:26,827 --> 00:42:31,327
いA + ですね = It is..., isn’t it? (e.g., 'It’s delicious, isn’t it?')

656
00:42:31,350 --> 00:42:34,722
Listening Test

657
00:42:34,722 --> 00:42:38,661
What are you planning to see?

658
00:42:38,661 --> 00:42:44,095
Vます + に + 行く = Go to do (e.g., 'I’m going to eat sushi')

659
00:42:44,118 --> 00:42:49,664
Listening Test

660
00:42:49,664 --> 00:42:56,330
Kiyomizu-dera, Kinkaku-ji, and Fushimi Inari.

661
00:42:56,330 --> 00:43:05,364
N1 + と + N2 = N1 and N2 (e.g., 'Kiyomizu Temple and Kinkaku-ji')

662
00:43:05,387 --> 00:43:09,287
Listening Test

663
00:43:09,287 --> 00:43:13,920
Are you planning to visit all of them in two days?

664
00:43:13,920 --> 00:43:20,239
Vる + 予定です = Plan to do (e.g., 'I plan to stay for two days and one night')

665
00:43:20,262 --> 00:43:22,362
Me too!

666
00:43:22,385 --> 00:43:26,285
Listening Test

667
00:43:26,285 --> 00:43:30,883
But I might not have enough time.

668
00:43:30,883 --> 00:43:37,163
Vない + かもしれません = Might not (e.g., 'It might not be enough')

669
00:43:37,186 --> 00:43:42,954
Listening Test

670
00:43:42,954 --> 00:43:49,888
Kyoto’s roads get congested, so trains are better than buses.

671
00:43:49,888 --> 00:43:59,277
N1 + より + N2 + のほうがいい = N2 is better than N1 (e.g., 'This place is better than a crowded one')

672
00:43:59,300 --> 00:44:01,648
Listening Test

673
00:44:01,648 --> 00:44:04,315
Is that so?

674
00:44:08,071 --> 00:44:11,738
Listening Test

675
00:44:11,738 --> 00:44:16,047
I thought buses would be more convenient.

676
00:44:16,047 --> 00:44:21,952
なA + だと思う = Think that... (e.g., 'I think it’s convenient')

677
00:44:21,975 --> 00:44:25,809
Listening Test

678
00:44:25,809 --> 00:44:30,309
It gets especially crowded in autumn.

679
00:44:30,309 --> 00:44:36,475
Vる + んです = [Explanation / Emphasis] (e.g., 'I especially like this one')

680
00:44:36,498 --> 00:44:40,002
Listening Test

681
00:44:40,002 --> 00:44:44,136
The subway would be faster.

682
00:44:44,136 --> 00:44:49,802
Vた + ほうがいい = Had better / It’s better to (e.g., 'You’d better take the subway—it’s faster')

683
00:44:49,825 --> 00:44:51,697
Listening Test

684
00:44:51,697 --> 00:44:53,797
Sounds good.

685
00:44:56,733 --> 00:45:00,867
Listening Test

686
00:45:00,867 --> 00:45:05,767
Where should I go on the first day?

687
00:45:05,767 --> 00:45:12,467
Vたら + いいですか = Should I...? (e.g., 'Should I go on the first day?')

688
00:45:12,490 --> 00:45:17,123
Listening Test

689
00:45:17,123 --> 00:45:22,625
I recommend visiting Fushimi Inari early in the morning.

690
00:45:22,625 --> 00:45:30,158
Vる + のをおすすめします = recommend doing V | 朝早く = early morning | おすすめ = recommendation

691
00:45:30,181 --> 00:45:34,048
Listening Test

692
00:45:34,048 --> 00:45:38,581
Is it because it gets crowded during the day?

693
00:45:38,581 --> 00:45:44,816
Vる + と = when/if V happens | 多い = many/much ↔ 少ない = few/little

694
00:45:44,839 --> 00:45:46,873
Yes, that's right.

695
00:45:46,896 --> 00:45:52,564
Listening Test

696
00:45:52,564 --> 00:45:59,358
Plus, if you're taking photos, mornings are the best for beautiful shots.

697
00:45:59,358 --> 00:46:08,591
Vる + なら = if doing V | 写真を撮る = take a photo | きれい = beautiful ≈ 美しい = beautiful

698
00:46:08,614 --> 00:46:12,547
Listening Test

699
00:46:12,547 --> 00:46:17,183
After that, we'll head to Kiyomizu-dera.

700
00:46:17,183 --> 00:46:23,533
その後 = after that

701
00:46:23,557 --> 00:46:26,723
Listening Test

702
00:46:26,723 --> 00:46:30,423
What about lunch?

703
00:46:30,423 --> 00:46:35,492
N + はどうしますか = What will you do about N? | お昼ご飯 = lunch

704
00:46:35,516 --> 00:46:39,460
Listening Test

705
00:46:39,460 --> 00:46:44,127
I'd love to try some delicious matcha sweets.

706
00:46:44,127 --> 00:46:50,502
Vたいです = want to do V | 美味しい = delicious ↔ 不味い = bad-tasting

707
00:46:50,525 --> 00:46:55,037
Listening Test

708
00:46:55,037 --> 00:47:00,411
There's a famous café near Kiyomizu-dera.

709
00:47:00,411 --> 00:47:07,745
N + に + N + があります = there is N in/at N | 近く = near ↔ 遠く = far | 有名 = famous

710
00:47:07,768 --> 00:47:10,744
Listening Test

711
00:47:10,744 --> 00:47:14,210
I'd love to check it out.

712
00:47:14,210 --> 00:47:18,994
Vて + みたいです = want to try doing V

713
00:47:19,018 --> 00:47:22,084
Listening Test

714
00:47:22,084 --> 00:47:25,634
Should we make a reservation?

715
00:47:25,634 --> 00:47:30,510
Vて + おいたほうがいい = had better do V in advance | 予約 = reservation

716
00:47:30,534 --> 00:47:35,567
Listening Test

717
00:47:35,567 --> 00:47:41,601
Check online to see if reservations are available.

718
00:47:41,601 --> 00:47:49,778
Plain form + かどうか = whether or not | 調べる = look up/search

719
00:47:49,801 --> 00:47:54,177
Listening Test

720
00:47:54,177 --> 00:47:59,410
I'm thinking of visiting Kinkaku-ji on the second day.

721
00:47:59,410 --> 00:48:06,510
Vよう + と思っています = thinking of doing V | 二日目 = the second day

722
00:48:06,533 --> 00:48:12,087
Listening Test

723
00:48:12,087 --> 00:48:18,787
Kinkaku-ji is stunning in the evening when the sunlight reflects off it.

724
00:48:18,787 --> 00:48:27,855
Vる + と = when/if V happens | 夕方 = evening | 太陽 = sun

725
00:48:27,879 --> 00:48:30,512
Listening Test

726
00:48:30,512 --> 00:48:33,545
That sounds amazing!

727
00:48:33,545 --> 00:48:37,712
素晴らしい = wonderful/splendid

728
00:48:37,735 --> 00:48:41,602
Listening Test

729
00:48:41,602 --> 00:48:46,143
I'd love to walk around in a kimono.

730
00:48:46,143 --> 00:48:52,376
Vて + みたいです = want to try doing V | 着物 = kimono | 借りる = borrow/rent ↔ 貸す = lend

731
00:48:52,399 --> 00:48:57,349
Listening Test

732
00:48:57,349 --> 00:49:03,268
You might need to book a kimono rental in advance.

733
00:49:03,268 --> 00:49:11,368
なA + かもしれません = might be... | レンタル = rental ≈ 借りること = renting | 事前 = in advance/prior

734
00:49:11,391 --> 00:49:13,897
Listening Test

735
00:49:13,897 --> 00:49:16,764
I see.

736
00:49:20,764 --> 00:49:24,498
Listening Test

737
00:49:24,498 --> 00:49:28,870
I'll make a reservation before I forget.

738
00:49:28,870 --> 00:49:34,861
Vない + うちに = before V happens/while not V | 忘れる = forget ↔ 覚える = remember

739
00:49:34,884 --> 00:49:40,118
Listening Test

740
